http://www.pastmon.org

PasTmon is a passive network application response time monitor.  It can
measure the response times and throughput of many of the Internet's most
used protocols such as http, irc, smtp and pop3...  The multi-threaded
plugin architecture and configurable transaction signatures makes
PasTmon a no-cost flexible solution for application response time
monitoring.

PasTmon is licensed under the GNU General Public License.

In this release:

Big performance improvements were made by implementing hash tables in
session tracking linked-lists.

Memory leaks in the generic and tcpsynack plugins were fixed.

An experimental signature file was added for tracking transactions in
the SSL protocol.

Improvements were made to the performance of the pastmonphp Web
interface.

MSIE's HTTP implementation is now supported.

PasTmon was ported to Tru64.

Many other bugfixes and improvements were also made.

- --

